Igor Cristoni wrote:
> 
> Hi all!
> I've just bought an alpha pc164 ux with 21164/533...I found that the riva tnt
> ghraphics card doesn't work at all...blank screen, not even the bios....anyone
> with the same problem? Must I change video card?

I have an lx164 and a tnt, 
same problem.

What I found out:
Alphabios will not even continue booting.
SRM will continue without video. You can use a serial console.

Problem is the tnt BIOS, which contains intel instructions that are
not supported by the x86 emulator from Digital.

Easy way out: exchange the tnt for a g200 card.
Eh... but you gotta know: g200's on PCI are becoming VERY rare.

Hard way out (emphasis on hard)  
* get on the x86emu mailing list at linuxlabs.com, and help
  integrate x86emu v0.1 back into MILO.
* make the xfree86-3.3.3.1 tnt driver 64bit safe
* grab g200/tnt glx from CVS and make the tnt glx module 64bit safe

I tried the hard way, now I use a g200/pci with my alpha.
I have now hw-accelerated 3d up and running (still bugs
in texturing and glDrawElements())

  Bram Stolk



