> Cool. 
>
> How about FreeBSD ? Tru64 is BSD 4.4, just like FBSD, so it would take 
> just a recompile :-)

That's... wrong.  Tru64 is OSF/1, the unix bits of which are 4.3-Reno,
not 4.4, for the most part, plus a lot of hacking by DEC.

It doesn't use the same object format as NetBSD or FreeBSD on the Alpha,
either; it uses ECOFF, whereas all other Unices on the alpha use ELF.

It probably wouldn't be hard, but I doubt it would just be "a recompile".

OTOH large numerical places like NASA Ames make extensive use of NetBSD
on large Alpha boxes; there would consequently seem to be demand for such
a product...

