What are all these guys talking about here? No one gave you an usefull
answer:
Look for the nearest/fastest mirror around that carries the
alpha-distribution. Get it with

wget -r ftp://ftp.mirror.com/.../.../redhat-6.0/alpha/

but make sure you have enough space on the HD. :)
Change into the just downloaded alpha-directory and make an iso-image
using

mkisofs -o alpha.raw -lrTv -V RedHat-6.0-Alpha -b milo/images/xxxx.img
alpha/

You probably don't need the boot-image (-b) option on the
alpha-distribution since milo might not work with it, but maybe it does in
your case. Finally burn the raw.img onto a cd using any burning-software
around and off you go.
This is the way I did with the i386 (bootable) and the alpha distribution
and it worked great, except for the networking problems with RedHat-6.0
after the installation on our Personal-Workstation 600.

