Actually, it works pretty cleanly here.  What *was* broken and stil is
*severely*, is the upgrade procedure itself.  After having finished
your upgrade, do

rpm --verify -a

All packages with missing files or bad-checksum files that are not
configuration files or otherwise supposed to be changed during normal
operation need to be reinstalled with

rpm -U --force packagename.rpm.

I suppose that installing RedHat 6.0 from scratch would not expose
this problem.


