ComputerCowboy wrote:

> Jon, Thanks for the steps.  I tried the strings in the sequence you outlined
> and I get to "Jumping to bootstrap code" and the system is hung.  I'm still
> having trouble figuring out how to make the ramdisk from the CDROM.  can I copy
> the files over in a windows environment or does it have to be Unix/Linux?  My
> alpha is basically unusable until I get RH 5.2-alpha loaded.  All I can do is
> work in the ARC or SRM environment.  I think I need to get the ramdisk thing
> done efore I go any further, can you offer any suggestions?  Appreciate the
> help.
>

You should be able to find radisk.exe, which is a

DOS program to copy floppy images, there is probably

a copy on your RH cd.

One problem I had setting up a similar system was

that I needed to use the "set MEMORY_SIZE 144"

as I had 144Mb installed instead of the default of 32Mb.

I currently boot the system by loading MILO from a floppy

with

        boot dva0           (SRM console)

Then

        set MEMORY_SIZE 144

        boot sda1:/vmlinuz.gz

If I recall correctly, as soon as I had MILO booting from

floppy I was able to install directly from the cd by booting

the appropriate cdrom kernel. One nice feature of MILO is that you

can do stuff like

        ls sda1:/kernels

from the MILO prompt.

Cheers,

    Dave

