OK,
   I am surprized that it was unable to boot from the cdrom.  Well to make 
the boot and ramdisk images you need either *NIX or an Windows/DOS machine.
Under ANY *NIX box mount the RedHat CD (or get the images from the RedHat 
site) the command is:
dd if=mikasa-s.img of=<raw device> bs=1440k
under Windows/DOS you can use the rawrite.exe program found in the 
dosutils directory of the RedHat cdrom.  Just run it and it will prompt 
you through making the disk.

The same commands work for making the ramdisk just use the 
/images/ramdisk.img instead of the mikasa-s.img.

Another possiblity is that you have some hardware that linux does not 
support (Mylex controller for example, it was added in RH6.0).  I believe 
you can get the Compaq list from http://www.compaq.com/linux/, there is 
another list of supported hardware from RedHat at:
http://www.redhat.com/corp/support/hardware/alpha/52/rh52-hardware-
alpha.html

Jon Ward



