This "Alpha arena" is of somewhat better quality (e.g. - decent signal-to
-noise ratio) than many other newsgroups.

Probably because actually *running* a Linux/Alpha box means some combination
of:
a) Expertise being deployed on some of the older Alpha systems (e.g. - some
of us run ancient Multia systems, and have few illusions about that variety
of machine being *vastly* more powerful than IA-32 brethren), and

b) Powerful Alpha boxes being fairly expensive, and thus out of the price
range for the "pimply-nosed teenagers with toys" demographic segment.

>Thank you all for the great info.  I have customers now wanting to know
>about Linux performance on the Alpha 64-bit architecture.  I admit that I
>know less than I should about the architecture itself.  I focus my hardware
