>the "64-bit processors are faster and that's all I need", or "as long as the
>OS is 64-bit capable then my systems will scream!"  I have some educating to
>do.

The *killer* question continues to be, and probably will remain, whether
or not the software that the users want to run will provide demonstrably
better results on Alpha.

For Oracle/Linux, the answer is "no," as Oracle is not available for any
Linux architecture other than IA-32.

Similar will be true for rather a lot of other software; there are not a
*lot* of commercial software offerings for Linux/Alpha at this point in
time, certainly not in comparison with the pretty vast selection for
IA-32.
