[Posted and mailed]

In article <3776747d.2017228@news.wish.net>,
	rwassens@thewatercooler.com writes:
> I want to cross-compile alph linux code on an i586 host. But I can't
> configure gcc-2.7.2.3 for target alpha-linux (is not supported). What
> do I have to do to make it work?

You won't have any luck to do that. It would work the other way round:
a compiler running on Linux Alpha which produces code for intel586

The problem is, that gcc (egcs, too!) assumes e.g., that a long on the
target fits in a long on the host. That's a gcc inherent problem, which
is not easy to fix.

PS: gcc-2.7.2.3 is very old. Use egcs instead (http://egcs.cygnus.com)

Bye,
Martin.

-- 
