Almost any ISA or PCI card should work.

: 2)	36 bit memory SIMMS (IMPORTANT, NOT 32 bit ), in FOURS, not
: pairs. This will cost quite a bit !
Sorry to correct you here but the AXPpci33 just has a 64bit memory bus and
so you only need two PS/2 SIMMs. But definetly you need true parity (i.e. 36
bit).

: 3)	A box to put it in
Be sure to use a case with good air flow. The CPU and especially the voltage
regulator get quite warm. You can add an additional fan in most PC cases
directly behind the front panel on the lower side (assuming a tower-like
case). This will then directly blow to the CPU and regulator.

: 4)	Something to load from
A floppy is just fine.

