  I had RH give me this error once on my PC164.  It turned out that the
mke2fs program was creating bad ext2 file systems.  I dropped out to the
shell by hitting ALT-F2, ran e2fsck on my target partitions, and then mv'ed
mke2fs to mke2fs.backup.  Then when the install tries to format the
partitions, it couldn't find mke2fs, and they mounted fine.  Oh, the RH
install makes and deletes device nodes, so there is no /dev/sda etc.  Check
the /tmp directory.
  P.S. I had no luck with the upgrade to RH6.0, it was really unstable.  I
ended up doing a full reinstall.

