All,
The DS10 uses lower performance chips to lower the cost of the system to a
level closer to a 'PC'. If you wanted to get two EV6 platforms @ 500MHz,
you should be looking at the XP1000, instead of the DS10 (intended to be a
web server, not the fastest uni-processor box - that's why it is call the
"Web Brick"). Other limitations come into play as well, such as PCI slots,
memory expansion, internal storage and mainly cost! DS10s are also a good
entry level Alpha machine that many more folks can afford vs DS20s.

Harry Heinisch
Compaq

