On Mon, 14 Jun 1999 12:31:33 -0500, charles <shultzjr@hpnc.com> wrote:
>I was hoping for something more in the $500-$1500 range.  From
>what I have seen, that is not possible yet.  And, if this is true,
>Intel will ALWAYS be a better buy, no matter how cool the
>Alpha architecture is.

Despite what another has said in this thread, a 21164 is still a
justifiable purchase if you don't absolutely need 21264 performance,
and is still competitive with Intel chips (A P3 will beat a 21164 in
integer by a not very large margin, but a 21164 will still win in
floating point).  164LX boards with a 533MHz 21164A were available for
around $1500 a year ago; you should be able to find them for much less
now.  Dual CPU will increase the price a bit, but it probably won't be
over $1500 (not sure, though).  164SX boards can be had *very* cheaply
if you look in the right places; I bought a 164SX+chip, not used, for
$250 on eBay a few months ago.  I'm unaware of any Intel chip+board
combo at that price that matches its performance even in integer,
unless high end P2's just got *really* cheap.

