Collin,

I got the same thing on my alphastation 255.

Here is what I did:

1. created two diskettes using rawrite.exe in the dosutils folder on the
cd, one containing generic.img. the other containing ramdisk.img from
the /images folder on the cd

2. booted to the milo prompt (I assume you can get this far)

3. at the milo prompt, I took out the milo disk, inserted the disk
containing generic.img and typed:

	boot fd0:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1

4. after a while a prompt will appear asking you to insert the disk
containing the ramdisk image
   take out the generic.img floppy, insert the ramdisk.img floppy and
press enter

5. the install procedure should start

good luck



