Well I havent tried this on a Mikasa but under 5.2 I found that setting the  
boot* variables was the only way to boot the CD directly.  Also you are not 
booting with the load_ramdisk=1 flag, that is required for installation.

Here is my recommendation, not only does this save some typing but it sets 
up booting after installation:

set auto_action HALT (this is a safety precaution)
set boot_file /kernels/mikasa-s.gz
set bootdef_dev dka400
set bootos_flags "root=/dev/scd0 bootfile=/kernels/mikasa-s.gz 
load_ramdisk=1"
boot

Let me know if this works.

