Renameing the kernel should have no effect on it as long as you tell
milo what the new name is, just as you have done. The '#'s are
displayed as the kernel is loaded into memory, that is normal. So as
long as the thing is booting up properly (I assume it is) there should
be no problem. 

Another thing, I don't know if you already know this or not, but
instead of typing 'boot sda1:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sda1' every time you
boot, In the ARC Firmware, you can go to the Supplementary Menu ->
Setup the System -> Manage Boot Selection menu -> Change a boot
selection, and in the selection where you are booting MILO, you can
place 'boot sda1:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sda1' under the OSLOADOPTIONS
variable.

	-Aravind Mikkilineni



