Fabrizio Petrini (fabrizio@lanl.gov) wrote:
: much better operating system than the native Unix. Given that this
: machine will be mainly used to run scientific applications I need to
: prove that the Linux C and Fortran compilers outperform  the native
: compilers. 

Just forget about this. Decpaq C and Fortran compilers produce alpha
executables which are usually faster by a substantial margin than 
gcc/g77 (or any other compiler available on alphas for that matter). 
The ratious anywhere from 0% to 200% has been quoted for different
programs, with 30% appearing to be the "normal" ballpark figure. YMMV -
it is quite possible (even if not very likely) that for your particular
application gcc/g77 will beat Decpaq compilers by a substantial margin.

In any event, a "much better operating system" is a matter of a very
subjective judgement. Depending on the mission requirements, personal
preferences, and the available on-site support either Linux or Tru64
(or WNT, or VMS for that matter) may be the "best" operating system
for your computer; asserting that the OS you personally happen to know
and like must be used because it is simply a "much better operating 
system" is an indication of ignorance at best, and zealotry at worst.

/Serge.P

