If I remember correctly (If not this is close), but do "srm help"

set boot_device   dka0   (the boot device as shown by a "show dev" at the
console)
set boot_file 2/vmlinux.gz    (2/ or your partition number that contains
your kernel)
set boot_flag  root=/dev/sda2    (assumes your root file system is on the
second partition)
set auto_action  boot   (will force a boot at the completion of power up
selftest)
or
set auto_action "halt"    (you will have to type "boot or b" followed by a
carriage return to force a boot after powerup selftest..


Hope this helps..
These commands are valid for most all srm consoles , there is also limited
help available on most console versions by typing help ? or help (Command
name)

JJ

