OK,
    to use the serial console, you must build a custom kernel with serial
console support. Then the tricky part, you have to delete /dev/console and
/dev/tty0 and create new ones with mkdev
refer to the Documentation directory under the linux kernel build directory
tree, and read Serial_Console.txt.   Then if a graphics card is detected it
will be the console device, if the graphics is NOT detected the serial
console will automatically become the console..No commands need to be passed
to the kernel at boot time unless you want BOTH to receive outputs.  works
for me on ds20, AS800, 3300,4000,4100, 7300, Miata's and MiataGL's..

You can only use a Video card that are is the SOC for the platform, they may
be detected, but the SRM console or AlphaBios may not have code to support
them (Ie they must be orderable).

JJ

