Riku Anttila <rixa@looksignatureforaddress.tut.fi> wrote:
:> 2) Completely replacing libm-6.1 with cpml doesn't work.  It breaks
:> various codes including gimp.  Creative use of LD_LIBRARY_PATH fixes
:> the problem.

: Many other applications are affected as well. What do you mean by creative
: use of LD_LIBRARY_PATH? Did you figure a way to fix the problem for good?
: I made a small script that links libm.so.6.1 to the desired math library,
: but I have to use it manually every time I want to change.

1) Create a directory containing the shared version of cpml renamed to be
(for example) /usr/local/lib/cpml/libm.so.6.1

2) setenv LD_LIBRARY_PATH /usr/local/lib/cpml:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH

3) setiathome

You could put staged 2 & 3 together in a simple script.  When an applications starts
it searches for shared libraries in the directories pointed to by LD_LIBRARY_PATH
before looking in the system defaults (e.g. /lib).

To check that it is working use strace to watch what files are being opened.

