wrote:

>I inherited a Multia SRM Console - model Vx40E-F3 - and I'm supposed to get
>Linux running on it.
>
>Right now, it won't even boot. I found some documents on the Internet that
>said to download the latest AlphaBIOS for my system onto a floppy and start
>there. But I can't even find the right version for this machine.

Download the firmware from
ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/interim/multia/udbupd38.img
and dd or rawrite it to a floppy.
Assuming your battery isn't dead, at the SRM prompt type ARC.
Insert the floppy and choose the update firmware option.
As far as I can tell it is only necessary if you want to use an IDE
disk. If you do you will have to upgrade the firmware before you plug
in the IDE drive or the machine will play dead.

Then you just follow the instructions in the RedHat manuals except
instead of typing 'boot floppy' in MILO you have to type 'boot
fd0:/vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1'.

Useful resource: www.alphalinux.org

Martin
