Success!

Not quite as your suggestion, but your reply gave me the impetus to get it
going as I thought I
was the only one trying to do this ;-)

For anyone reading this trying to get a alphapc164UX booting linux from scsi
disk id0 set the nvram to:

osloadfilename  \
loadidentifier RedHat Linux 5.2    (doesn't matter)
osloadoptions  boot sda1:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sda1
systempartition  scsi(1) disk(0) rdisk(0) partition(1)
osloadpartition  scsi(1) disk(0) rdisk(0) partition(3)
osloader scsi(1) disk(0) rdisk(0) partition(3)\ldmilo.exe

A  couple of other points:

I set disk druid to sda6 for the dos milo hdd partition, but the ARC Bios sees
it as sda3 !
You can check this with the configuration options, highlight the disk itself,
and there is an option to list the files. Then you get a choice which
partition, it only works on dos/FAT partitions, and for some reason sda6 turns
out to be sda3.

I created sda6 and dd 'd the milo diskette image into it, as the RH alpha
guide suggested, but it would not work until I copied the file ldmilo.exe and
milo on to the hdd from the floppy using the bios copy command (same sub-menu
as the dir command)

Hope this saves anyone else pulling their hair out for 3 days trying to work
it out!

Pi





