Jameel Akari wrote:

> Mathieu Millet wrote:
>
> > So let's start with RH 5.2. I'm able to install everything.
> > But when I launch Xfree the network stops working after a preiod from
> > immediately to 15 minutes.
> > ping localhost works and ifconfig reports no error. but ping <something
> > else> doesn't work. If I run ifdown eth0 then ifup eth0, the network is back
> > online.
> >

    Removing the tulip driver and installing the DE4x5 driver instead seems to have
fixed my problem.  It's been running the past 11 hours this way without needing an
ifdown/ifup kick to unlock it.


>     I had this same problem intermittently with RH5.2 as well on my UDB.  Didn't

    This still isn't explained.. maybe I got a newer tulip driver with some update
that I don't remember.


>     There's a patch for ping around.  Is there maybe an updated netkit package
> out yet?  Probably not much difference between 5.2 and 6.0 netkit anyway.  It
> frightens me that RedHat managed to add a new bug to ping in the first place.
>

    Is there a fixed ping binary available?  Also, I see the unaligned trap errors
with in.identd as well.


> > Does anyone has experience the same thing? Or any explanations at least??
>
>     I was leaning towards replacing my ethernet adaptor, but since you have the
> same problem, I'm not so sure.

    Looks like the driver is at least part of the problem.  Just to be thorough,
what you should try is:

> ifdown eth0    (to make the tulip module unused)
> rmmod tulip    (remove current Tulip NIC module)
> insmod de4x5.o  (insert the de4x5 module instead)
> ifup eth0   (might not need to do this?)

You should see in your messages that the module initialized, and it'll list what the
IRQ is of your NIC.


-Jameel





