I've found that rawriting the ramdisk.img for Alphas hasn't worked for
me properly.  The way I do it now that seems to have solved the problem
is the following incantation under linux:

dd if=ramdisk.img of=/dev/fd0 bs=1440k

Note that without the bs=1440k addition at the end, the ramdisk has
failed on some occations, so put it in.

